.TH OMNI-SECRET 1 "October 2026" "omni-term-ai" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omni-secret \\- store and retrieve Omni Term AI API keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omni-secret backend
.br
.B omni-secret get
.I name
.br
.B omni-secret store
.I name
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads and writes harness API keys in the OS secret store.
A missing key is not planted as an empty value.
.PP
Names:
.BR xai ,
.BR deepseek ,
.BR anthropic ,
.BR openai ,
.BR github ,
.BR gemini ,
.BR azure .
They map to
.BR XAI_API_KEY ,
.BR DEEPSEEK_API_KEY ,
.BR ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ,
.BR OPENAI_API_KEY ,
.BR GH_TOKEN ,
.BR GEMINI_API_KEY ,
and
.BR AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B omni-secret backend
Prints the backend in use:
.BR secret-tool ,
.BR security ,
.BR pass ,
or
.BR file .
.TP
.B omni-secret get \fIname\fR
Prints the stored secret, or nothing if it was never stored.
.TP
.B omni-secret store \fIname\fR
Reads the secret from the terminal and stores it.
The secret is not passed on the command line.
secret-tool items use the attribute
.B service=omni-term-ai
so they do not collide with another program's
.B api
attribute. A key stored before that change is still found, and copied
forward on read.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/omni-term-ai/secrets/
.RS
Used only when no OS secret backend is available. Mode 0600.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR omni-config (1),
.BR omni-exec (1),
.BR launch-ai-workspace (1)
